    {
      "path": "/projects/2/description",
      "value": "The project focused on automating and streamlining the processing of debit and credit transactions received through the ACH 825 sub-ledger, a core component of Citi Bank’s retail banking services. The objective was to ensure accurate and efficient handling of financial transactions based on market, transaction amount, and reason type, as defined in the ACH 825 requests. I was actively involved in requirement gathering, preparing detailed Business Requirement Documents (BRDs), and designing process flow diagrams using Microsoft Visio. My role also included coordinating with the technical team for requirement clarifications, managing deliverables, and collaborating closely with business stakeholders through one-on-one discussions and workshops. Additionally, I participated in weekly client meetings to provide status updates, assisted team members in understanding business functionality, and conducted demonstrations and presentations for customer SMEs. Post- implementation, I documented the finalized process flows to support smooth transition and operational consistency. This initiative enhanced transaction accuracy, improved process, transparency, and strengthened the overall efficiency of Citi Bank’s ACH 825 sub-ledger operations. and version control support.",
